      "shared_perspectives": "German media across the spectrum agree that the war in Ukraine has made it politically unavoidable for Germany to close the gap to NATO’s 2 percent spending guideline and to accelerate a comprehensive modernization of the Bundeswehr, especially in procurement and digitalisation. They also converge on the view that structural reforms – such as improving acquisition processes, expanding reserve concepts and strengthening cyber‑defence – are essential to make the armed forces capable of fulfilling both NATO commitments and domestic security tasks. Finally, there is a shared perception that a more robust alliance posture and a clearer strategic orientation toward collective defence are now central pillars of Germany’s security policy.",
